### Login client of the realm (realm owner): run user_auth.http first to get auth_token

### Get the login client (clientId = realm name)
GET http://localhost:8282/api/admin/login-client
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}

### Set the redirect URIs and web origins (replaces the three lists)
PUT http://localhost:8282/api/admin/login-client
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "redirectUris": ["https://app.example.com/*", "http://localhost:5173/*"],
  "postLogoutRedirectUris": ["https://app.example.com/"],
  "webOrigins": ["+"]
}

### Set the default catalogs: in every token of the client, the others only with scope=<catalog>
PUT http://localhost:8282/api/admin/login-client
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "redirectUris": ["https://app.example.com/*", "http://localhost:5173/*"],
  "postLogoutRedirectUris": ["https://app.example.com/"],
  "webOrigins": ["+"],
  "defaultCatalogs": ["products"]
}

### Refused (400): a lone wildcard would accept any site
PUT http://localhost:8282/api/admin/login-client
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "redirectUris": ["*"],
  "postLogoutRedirectUris": [],
  "webOrigins": []
}
